  "body": "### Summary\n\nWanted by LOT-023 (#51): the MP list parser has no capture of a row whose thread is **closed for the member** (the member left or was excluded); #118 covers only the ignore icon states.\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: MP list (logged in) containing a row of a thread closed for the member, anonymized.\n\n### Sources\n\n- LOT-023 spec (pending capture list); #118 for the neighbouring ignore-icon state\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Anonymized capture of the MP list with such a row, plus legacy oracle output.\n- [ ] Row removed from the Capture backlog; LOT-023 spec updated.\n\nRules: LOT-001 kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), anonymize every free-text field, independent leak check before any push, never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36), legacy oracle when a parser consumes it, one PR per batch of captures, the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog in `docs/LOTS.md`. Write captures need the operator approval first.",
